{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FaPFqyjkHBxhLypiuJ8EwQ","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md b/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md\nindex ce995941..dcf920bb 100644\n--- a/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md\n+++ b/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md\n@@ -14,3 +14,4 @@ Each line below is a human's citation of the act that authorised a refresh absor\n - 2026-08-23 — refreshed under approval ref: **the owner's in-session act 2026-08-23 — \"OI-61: I agree with the recommendation, let's see where it lands, and I approve of the other spine changes surfaced in open-items.html\" — recorded at docs/log.d/2026-08-23-oi61-rule-and-spine-approval.md** (7 registry file(s)).\n - 2026-08-24 — refreshed under approval ref: **the owner's in-session directive 2026-08-24 — \"… and then I will approve of the spine changes and lock in on option e of OI-62\" (elision: the dropped opening clause concerns session logistics, quoted in full in the fragment) — recorded at docs/log.d/2026-08-24-oi62-rule-and-spine-approval.md** (7 registry file(s)).\n - 2026-08-30 — refreshed under approval ref: **WI-508 close sitting 2026-08-30 — absorbs WI-520's already-merged CMP-006 kitlib listing (secret_classes.py); see docs/log.d/2026-08-30-wi508-slice6-spine-approval-and-close.md** (7 registry file(s)).\n+- 2026-09-04 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (ref: WI-590); test-cases.toml (ref: WI-590). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.\ndiff --git a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\nindex fe9c0412..f00d9b7c 100644\n--- a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n+++ b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n@@ -2199,7 +2199,7 @@ code_symbol = \"scopes/render/targets/_extra/main\"\n detail = \"\"\"One file per review scope under docs/reviews/rollup/<train>.md, compiled from the round files that scope carries: ordinal, phase, reviewed sha, parsed verdict word, finding count and filename, one row each. The scope SET is the train field the round-file name parser itself returns, taken over every round file found under docs/reviews/ - not the directory layout, because a second notion of what a review scope is can disagree with the first: enumerating directories skipped the flat pre-train layout that parser supports, which produced an empty rollup directory AND a --check calling it fresh against the same empty target set. That layout has no directory to be named after, so its rollup takes a reserved stem, and the one name collision that leaves is REFUSED by name on both the check and the write arm rather than resolved by a last write - two scopes sharing one output file leave the other permanently stale. The scope is the TRAIN and not the work item, because a traincar is one review scope - a worker schedules its round only once every assigned item is built and the round covers the combined train diff, so a per-item rollup would have to invent a slice of a round that does not exist. Declared in the toolchain file's generated section, freshness-gated by --check at the commit floor, and standing down on a work branch with the rest of the trunk-owned artifacts - the one member of that set whose SOURCE a branch necessarily writes, since the round files are a lane's own committed evidence. THE WRITER THAT CLOSES THAT CIRCLE IS THE TRUNK STEP'S REGEN SET, named by the id it carries there: the `verdict-rollup` row, armed by the presence of docs/reviews/ and skipped with a printed notice wherever that directory is absent, a LEAF whose position in the dependency order is therefore free. Membership in that set is part of THIS contract and not an implementation accident, because it is the only thing that makes the exclusive-writer clause above true: a work branch stands the freshness check down and commits the round files, so a trunk step that does not run this generator leaves the artifact written by nobody, and the first commit floor that reads it reds on a staleness no lane is permitted to clear. The generator OWNS that directory rather than only writing into it: --check reports an absent file, a diverged one and an EXTRA one - a retired review scope keeping its rollup is the same lie as an out-of-date one - on normalized line endings, and the WRITE path prunes the extra in the pass that writes the rest. Both halves or neither: reporting a file the regenerator would never touch made the remedy the failure message names unable to clear the failure, which on a step sitting at the commit floor and in the trunk freshness set is an unbreakable red under a misleading instruction. It names NO governing verdict: governing is tree identity, a question about a branch's current tree that can only be answered against a repository at a moment, so every row here is a fact about a file.\"\"\"\n rationale = \"\"\"The hand-authored per-item rollup was the merge gate's only input and nothing in the kit wrote it, so every mechanized lane stopped at a human - and because it paraphrased evidence that already existed, it was also the one artifact in the tree that was neither generated, checked nor declared while the doctrine everywhere else refuses that shape. Splitting the roles is what makes both halves honest: the gate reads the evidence, and the summary a human genuinely wants to read becomes derived state that cannot drift from it. Writing a governing verdict into the file would rebuild the retired artifact under a new name - a checked-in summary that reads as authority and is stale the moment the branch moves - so the file states facts about files and stops.\"\"\"\n test_refs = \"TC-206\"\n-status = \"Drafted\"\n+status = \"Approved\"\n component = \"CMP-009\"\n phase = 5\n \ndiff --git a/docs/test/test-cases.toml b/docs/test/test-cases.toml\nindex 2e927881..ee05ee32 100644\n--- a/docs/test/test-cases.toml\n+++ b/docs/test/test-cases.toml\n@@ -2096,7 +2096,7 @@ tier = \"Smoke\"\n expected = \"Satisfies SR-170: the per-review-scope rollup is written by a regenerator the serial merge step runs and never by a work branch, its freshness is gated with two answers, and the artifact states that it is not the gate's input\"\n automated = \"Yes\"\n evidence = \"\"\"tests/test_verdict_record.py::test_the_rollup_is_generated_and_its_check_has_two_answers; tests/test_trunk_step.py::test_regen_really_writes_the_verdict_rollup; tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py::test_every_declared_generated_artifact_has_an_enforcer; tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py::test_every_wired_enforcer_is_a_real_step_and_runs_in_the_commit_floor; tests/test_check_lane.py::test_every_declared_freshness_step_is_skipped\"\"\"\n-status = \"Drafted\"\n+status = \"Approved\"\n phase = 5\n \n [test.TC-207]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48d2ea8d-10f4-4218-9045-50743face1da","uuid":"b56a245d-f12d-4979-b4c5-6e2ec639c9cb","timestamp":"2026-09-04T20:48:03.814Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md b/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md\nindex ce995941..dcf920bb 100644\n--- a/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md\n+++ b/docs/archive/last_approved/README.md\n@@ -14,3 +14,4 @@ Each line below is a human's citation of the act that authorised a refresh absor\n - 2026-08-23 — refreshed under approval ref: **the owner's in-session act 2026-08-23 — \"OI-61: I agree with the recommendation, let's see where it lands, and I approve of the other spine changes surfaced in open-items.html\" — recorded at docs/log.d/2026-08-23-oi61-rule-and-spine-approval.md** (7 registry file(s)).\n - 2026-08-24 — refreshed under approval ref: **the owner's in-session directive 2026-08-24 — \"… and then I will approve of the spine changes and lock in on option e of OI-62\" (elision: the dropped opening clause concerns session logistics, quoted in full in the fragment) — recorded at docs/log.d/2026-0